import json
from pathlib import Path
r=json.loads(Path('logs/intermediate_50m_comparison_20261018.json').read_text())
r['lineage_status']='Cadence-1 TPU intermediates; do not connect them to the cadence-10 python final. Matching final is a candidate supported by weight proximity and matching settings, not a recorded training lineage.'
r['excluded_runs']={'50m_2.5b':'Different task settings and unequal embedding/output weights. Not used for backend conclusions.','legacy_separate_phases':'Excluded per user instruction.'}
Path('logs/intermediate_50m_comparison_20261018.json').write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2))
end=json.loads(Path('logs/intermediate_50m_cadence1_final_20261018.json').read_text())
lines=['# Intermediate 50M checkpoint inspection — 18 October 2026','','## Eligibility and provenance','','The user explicitly warned against mixing old separate Phase A/B/C checkpoints into the unified COROSred comparison. The selected CUDA Lightning and TPU Python intermediates explicitly declare `corosred.unified=True` and `phase=unified`, with matching model architecture and main task settings. Their SHA-256 hashes match the pinned HF revision below. These flags are evidence of intended configuration, not proof of the exact historical training source.','','- HF repo: https://huggingface.co/Kazenowoko/telos',f'- Revision: `{r["hf_revision"]}`','- CUDA files last uploaded 14 September 2026; TPU Python files uploaded 18 September in a commit describing LR and schedule cadence 1. Upload dates are not training dates.','- Older `50m_2.5b` experiment excluded: differing task settings and embedding/output tensors that disagree despite the tied-embedding flag. Its saved Adam state is not used to explain the later backend gap.','- Separate-phase legacy models excluded.','','## Important lineage mismatch','','The `50m_python` intermediates save scheduler cadence 1 and explicit cadence-1 configuration, while the final checkpoint in that same directory saves cadence 10 and lacks those explicit settings. Do not connect that final to the intermediates as a verified continuous run.','','Relative weight L2 distance from the step-12,000 intermediate (output weight alias excluded):','','| Candidate | Relative distance | Weight cosine |','|---|---:|---:|']
for row in json.loads(Path('logs/intermediate_50m_lineage_distances_20261018.json').read_text()):
 lines.append(f'| `{row["path"]}` | {row["relative_l2_distance_from_python_step12000"]:.6f} | {row["weight_cosine"]:.6f} |')
lines+=['','The local `50m_tpu_lrcadence_schedstep1` endpoint is strongly compatible with the intermediates by weight proximity and settings. That is an inferred candidate relationship, not a proven resume chain. It is not present in the pinned HF inventory and is identified by its local file hash in the separate evaluation JSON.','','## Common-fixture measurements','','All evaluations reuse the prior exact seed-42 fixture: 16 sequences of 512 tokens (8,192 input tokens), four microbatches, CPU FP32, dropout disabled. Causal and bidirectional infill attention are explicit. Infill loss uses masked target positions only. These are endpoint gradients under the current common evaluator, excluding reliability loss; they do not reconstruct the historical mixed objective, clipping, or Adam updates. This slice is not established to be document-disjoint from training.','','| Checkpoint | Step | Causal CE | Infill CE | Task-gradient cosine |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for label,v in r['models'].items():
 lines.append(f'| {label} | {v["metadata"]["step"]} | {v["causal"]["ce"]:.5f} | {v["infill"]["ce"]:.5f} | {v["gradient_geometry"]["all_backbone"]["causal_infill_cosine"]:.4f} |')
lines.append(f'| TPU cadence-1 candidate final | {end["metadata"]["step"]} | {end["causal"]["ce"]:.5f} | {end["infill"]["ce"]:.5f} | {end["gradient_geometry"]["all_backbone"]["causal_infill_cosine"]:.4f} |')
lines+=['','## Bounded interpretation','','- The quality deficit is already present at TPU step 4,000: both losses are worse even than CUDA step 1,271 on these identical inputs. Nearby-step comparisons also favor CUDA. This establishes a deficit by the first eligible TPU save, not its onset or training cause.','- TPU continues improving between its observed intermediate saves. These sparse checkpoints cannot rule out instability between saves or prove a convergence floor.','- Overall causal/infill gradients are positively aligned at each measured intermediate. Layer-level geometry is retained in JSON; endpoint alignment does not rule out historical training-time conflicts.','- Historical moments are absent from the selected TPU intermediates. The older experiment with moments is excluded from causal comparison.','- No accelerator time or training was used. Production training code was not changed. Four existing regression tests of the shared evaluator passed.','','## Artifacts','','- `logs/intermediate_50m_comparison_20261018.json`: seven checkpoint measurements, configs, scheduler state, gradients and HF provenance.','- `logs/intermediate_50m_cadence1_final_20261018.json`: local candidate endpoint measurement.','- `logs/intermediate_50m_lineage_distances_20261018.json`: candidate weight-distance measurements.','- `scratch/backend_parity/hf_50m_inventory.json` and `hf_50m_file_history.json`: pinned HF inventory and file history.','','The productive next target is the unified trainer path before step 4,000. Saved checkpoints narrow the interval; they do not yet distinguish BF16 kernels, optimizer execution, clipping, or other training behavior.']
p=Path('research/intermediate_50m_inspection_2026-10-18.md');p.write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n');print(p)
